/A 980 0 R
/Alt (Concept map graphic comparing perceived risks and benefits of conventional robots and soft robots for social assistance. Central risks for both types include loss of therapist jobs, risk of dependency, lack of empathy, unknown reactions, and unrealistic learning. Benefits identified include non-judgmental feedback, learning, emotion recognition, infinite patience, low risk of injury, animal protection, and supportive qualities. Each risk and benefit is grouped in color-coded hexagons or ovals, with labeled arrows connecting related concepts to both robot categories.)
/ID (ID.0152)
