/A 983 0 R
/Alt (Concept map graphic illustrating risks and benefits of rescue robots. Risks are in red hexagons, including complexity of the problem, lack of safety net, problems with contacting, black box, thought process not comprehensible, developer bias, and bias of algorithms. Risks connect to rescue robot, which also connects to benefits in green ellipses, such as deciphering incomprehensible patterns, improved approach, accessibility of inaccessible places, flexibility, relief for rescue workers, better support possible, and new approaches. "Calming the injured" is in a yellow rectangle linked to risks, while benefits link to detailed concepts through green lines.)
